-- title:
--   Support torsion gives approximate shore-swap maps in every positive dimension
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a graph on a finite set and suppose its support space $\mathcal S(H)$ has torsion data: a point $p$, paths $a:p\to\tau p$ and $b=\tau a:\tau p\to p$, and a positive integer $k$ with $(a*b)^k$ nullhomotopic relative to endpoints. Let $d\ge1$ and let $\mathbb Z^d$ act freely and continuously on a zero-dimensional Polish space $X$. Then
--   $$\forall\varepsilon>0\ \exists f:X\to\mathcal S(H)\text{ continuous with finite range},\quad
--   d(f(e_i\cdot x),\tau(f(x)))<\varepsilon\quad\forall x,i.$$
--   The vertex set and action space may lie in independent universes; $\tau$ interchanges the probability shores.
-- source:
--   Ruijun Wang, Continuous graph homomorphisms of higher dimensional abelian group actions, arXiv:2609.39824v1 (30 September 2026), Sections 2–7, supporting construction for Theorem 1.4 and Proposition 7.1; https://arxiv.org/html/2609.39824v1. Formalization-specific helper: AbelianTargets/PositiveTheorems.lean, lines 20–51; SHA256 72f36f05675ae84f52f933d00ea9df29391a52807814b57263eb081d5b1a0fc6.

